  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Retries",
      "items": [
        "The retrying HTTP client repeats the whole round trip, so the auth round-tripper runs, and fetches the header, on every attempt",
        "Defaults: up to 4 retries, exponential backoff from 1 s to 30 s",
        "Once retries are used up, the default error handler (PassthroughErrorHandler) hands back the last response or transport error",
        "WithoutRetries removes this layer; WithRetryMax, WithRetryWait, WithCheckRetry, WithBackoff and WithErrorHandler tune it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authorization header",
      "items": [
        "AuthSource.Init runs once in NewWithAuthSource",
        "AuthSource.Header runs on every request; a header the caller already set is kept",
        "A failing auth source fails the attempt before anything is sent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One error model",
      "items": [
        "A 2xx response decodes into the typed result",
        "An error status becomes one APIError with status code, raw body and decoded error model, also the last 429 or 5xx once retries are used up",
        "Transport and context errors, and a 2xx body that fails to decode, are wrapped with %w, not turned into APIError",
        "Escape-hatch callers enter at the generated service and can call WrapAPIError themselves"
      ]
    }
  ]
